{"adr":"Decision: one in-browser BookingService (lib/booking) holds every rule over localStorage, with an injectable clock and storage. contracts/openapi.yaml is served in the browser by a local fetch adapter, and screens use only the generated lib/api client over it, so there are no network calls.\nPrecedence (fixes critic gaps): book checks not_found > cancelled_by_studio > class_has_started > outside_booking_window > already_booked > class_full > overlap > limit_reached. Cancel and leave check record state (invalid_booking_state) before class_has_started.\nA Booked or Waitlisted record wins over Disabled in the action state, with canChange=false and a reason once the class has started. Undo only works on a Booked record less than 5 s old (otherwise undo_expired or invalid_booking_state) and subtracts 1 from the booked count.\nSeed sessions use London wall-clock times (DST-safe). Weeks roll forward without touching stored data. Corrupt or old-version storage is re-seeded; storage that can't be read gives storage_failure and Retry.\nPromotion toasts come from stored PromotionNotices that are acknowledged once. Schedule and My Bookings state (day, week, filters, tab, from) lives in the URL so Back restores it.","chosen":"OPT-B","complexity":"L","header":{"createdAt":"2026-10-06T23:36:30.081Z","inputsHash":"","kind":"plan","producedBy":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","stage":"plan"},"runId":"20261006-boutique-fitness-studio-class-b497","schemaVersion":1},"newDependencies":[],"options":[{"id":"OPT-A","simplest":true,"summary":"Screen containers call an in-browser BookingService module directly through React hooks. No contract client.","tradeoffs":"Least code (no transport adapter). But it breaks the rule that the web app talks to the API only through the generated lib/api client, the web tests cannot run against contract examples, and a future real API would mean rewriting every container."},{"id":"OPT-B","simplest":false,"summary":"All rules live in an in-browser BookingService (lib/booking) over localStorage with an injectable clock. The contract (contracts/openapi.yaml) is served inside the browser by a local fetch adapter (lib/booking/local-api.ts). Containers call only the generated lib/api client, wired to that adapter, so nothing goes over the network.","tradeoffs":"About 300 extra lines for the adapter and DTO mapping. In return it follows the contract, keeps PII in the browser (NFR-12), lets unit tests call the service directly (REQ-60) and lets screen tests run against the contract examples. A real backend could later replace the adapter without touching the screens."},{"id":"OPT-C","simplest":false,"summary":"Build a real backend API repo with server-side persistence. The web app uses the generated client over HTTP.","tradeoffs":"Out of scope: the spec rules out any backend or database, and member data would leave the browser (breaks NFR-12). It also needs hosting beyond a static app in one region (NFR-11)."}],"protectedPathsDeclared":["package.json"],"stubs":[{"content":"export type ClassType = \"Yoga\" | \"Pilates\" | \"HIIT\" | \"Spin\" | \"Boxing\";\nexport type Intensity = \"Low\" | \"Medium\" | \"High\";\nexport type Room = \"Studio A\" | \"Studio B\" | \"Spin Room\";\nexport type TimeOfDay = \"Morning\" | \"Afternoon\" | \"Evening\";\nexport type SessionStatus = \"Scheduled\" | \"Cancelled by studio\";\nexport type BookingStatus = \"Booked\" | \"Waitlisted\" | \"Cancelled\" | \"Attended\" | \"Cancelled by studio\";\n\nexport interface Instructor {\n  id: number;\n  name: string;\n  bio: string;\n  avatarUrl: string;\n}\n\nexport interface WhatToBringItem {\n  title: string;\n  note: string;\n}\n\nexport interface Session {\n  id: number;\n  name: string;\n  type: ClassType;\n  intensity: Intensity;\n  instructorId: number;\n  room: Room;\n  /** ISO UTC date-time */\n  startsAt: string;\n  /** 30, 45, 60 or 75 */\n  durationMin: number;\n  capacity: number;\n  bookedCount: number;\n  waitlistCount: number;\n  descrip