in waitlist\n          allOf:\n            - $ref: \"#/components/schemas/Session\"\n","path":"contracts/openapi.yaml","reason":"The shared API contract for the web app and the API side. The generated lib/api client is built from it, and the web tests run against its examples."}],"tasks":[{"approach":"install the packages and build the app once: the scaffold compiles as written","conventions":["Keep the factory-generated design tokens (CSS variables) in app/globals.css as the single source of colours, type, radii and spacing","Do not restyle generated pages or kit components"],"dependsOn":[],"exemplars":["app/globals.css","app/layout.tsx"],"fileScope":["app/layout.tsx","package.json","app/globals.css"],"id":"TASK-1","newFileKind":false,"plannedLoc":10,"reqs":["REQ-51","REQ-52","REQ-53","REQ-54","REQ-59"],"title":"Design system: install and build the generated scaffold"},{"approach":"Implement the stub files. time.ts: use Intl.DateTimeFormat with timeZone Europe/London and hourCycle h23. formatTime gives HH:mm (AC-2.2 17:30Z -> \"18:30\"). londonDate and todayInLondon (AC-2.1). weekStartOf (Monday). londonDateTimeToUtc turns a London wall-clock time into UTC, working out the offset per date so DST weeks come out right. dayChipLabel gives \"Mon 12\", dayGroupLabel gives Today/Tomorrow/\"Thu 15 Oct\", shortDayTime gives \"Mon 07:00\". timeOfDayOf: Morning <12:00, Afternoon 12:00–16:59, Evening >=17:00. labels.ts: availabilityLabel follows REQ-32 exactly (Cancelled / \"Full · N on waitlist\" / \"1 spot left\" / \"Only N left\" / \"N spots left\"), capacityAriaLabel gives \"N of M spots left\", bookingBadge gives Booked / Waitlisted #N / Attended / Cancelled / Late cancel / Cancelled by studio. errors.ts: error codes plus plain-language default messages. bookingError() builds a BookingFailure. BookingStorageError is thrown when storage can't be read. storage.ts: KeyValueStorage interface, createMemoryStorage, browserStorage, readState and writeState with JSON under STORAGE_KEY and schemaVersion 1. readState returns null when the key is empty, the JSON is corrupt or the version doesn't match (the caller re-seeds), and throws BookingStorageError when getItem throws. writeState lets setItem errors pass through. seed.ts: 5 instructors with name, bio and avatarUrl. generateWeekSessions is deterministic, seeded by weekStart: at least 20 sessions per week, all 5 types, rooms Studio A/Studio B/Spin Room, durations 30/45/60/75, a 2–4 sentence description, a non-empty whatToBring, at least 2 full, at least 2 with 1–3 left and at least 1 Cancelled by studio per week. generateSeed(now) builds the current and next week plus Alex's records: 2 Booked on future sessions that start at least 15 min and at most 7 days from now, don't overlap and are counted in bookedCount; 1 Waitlisted on a full session with position <= waitlistCount; 3 Attended on extra history sessions dated before the current week. None of them is on a studio-cancelled session. rollForward(state, now) appends any missing current or next week (tracked in seededWeeks) with fresh ids and no bookings, and never changes existing sessions, bookings or counts (AC-62.1–62.3).","conventions":["Pure TypeScript modules, no React and no direct window access except browserStorage()","Integer ids everywhere; date-times are ISO UTC strings; calendar dates are YYYY-MM-DD in Europe/London","No Math.random or Date.now: take `now` or a clock as an argument so tests are deterministic"],"dependsOn":["TASK-1"],"exemplars":["lib/utils.ts","contracts/openapi.yaml"],"fileScope":["lib/booking/types.ts","lib/booking/errors.ts","lib/booking/time.ts","lib/booking/storage.ts","lib/booking/seed.ts","lib/booking/labels.ts"],"id":"TASK-2","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":520,"reqs":["REQ-2","REQ-3","REQ-4","REQ-5","REQ-32","REQ-62"],"title":"Booking domain foundation: types, London time, storage, seed generator and roll-forward, labels, errors"},{"approach":"Constructor: options.clock defaults to () => new Date() and options.storage to browserStorage(). Run readState; null means generateSeed(now). Then rollForward and persist. A BookingStorageError from the read is passed up to the caller. Derived status: a Booked record on an ended session reads as Attended. A Booked or Waitlisted record on a studio-cancelled session reads as Cancelled by studio. A Waitlisted record on an ended session is hidden from both lists. book precedence: not_found > cancelled_by_studio > class_has_started (start <= now) > outside_booking_window (start > now+168h, or start < now+15min) > already_booked (Booked or Waitlisted exists) > class_full > overlap (half-open ranges, message \"You're already booked for <name> at <HH:mm>–<HH:mm>.\") > limit_reached (10 Booked on sessions not yet started, message \"You've reached the limit of 10 upcoming classes.\"). On success: bookedCount+1 and a new record with createdAt. joinWaitlist uses the same checks up to already_booked, then not_full when spots are free. It skips the overlap and limit checks, sets position = waitlistCount+1 and adds 1 to waitlistCount. cancel: not_found > invalid_booking_state (derived status not Booked) > class_has_started. It sets Cancelled with lateCancel = start-now < 2h (exactly 120 min is free). If waitlistCount > 0 it subtracts 1 from waitlistCount, otherwise 1 from bookedCount. leaveWaitlist: invalid_booking_state unless Waitlisted, then class_has_started. It sets Cancelled with lateCancel false, subtracts 1 from waitlistCount, and moves other positions up only for Alex's own record (others are counts). undoBooking: invalid_booking_state unless Booked, undo_expired if now-createdAt > 5000 ms. It deletes the record and subtracts 1 from bookedCount. isLateCancellation(booking): start-now < 2h. simulateOtherMemberCancellation implements REQ-21/22 exactly: if Alex is at position 1 and eligible (no overlap, under the limit, start >= now+15min), Alex becomes Booked with position null and skipReason null, waitlistCount-1, and a PromotionNotice(seen=false) is pushed. If not eligible, Alex stays at #1 with skipReason {code, message naming the class or the limit}; then waitlistCount-1 if others are waiting (waitlistCount > 1), otherwise bookedCount-1. If Alex is at position > 1, Alex's position-1 and waitlistCount-1. With no waitlist, bookedCount-1. filters.ts: filterSessions does OR within a group, AND across groups, empty group matches all, sorted by startsAt, and keeps studio-cancelled sessions. getSchedule(date, filters) returns the sessions for that London date. getWeek(weekStart) gives 7 DaySummary with hasSessions. getMyBookings: upcoming = Booked/Waitlisted on sessions not ended, ascending, grouped by dayGroupLabel. past = Attended, Cancelled and Cancelled by studio, newest first. getStats follows REQ-30 (streak counts Mon–Sun weeks back from the current week, or from last week if this week has none yet). getActionState: a held record wins (booked / waitlisted with skipReason, canChange=false and reason \"Class has started\" once started). Otherwise Disabled with reason 'Cancelled by studio' / 'Class has started' / 'Booking opens 7 days before class' / 'Booking closes 15 minutes before class', then join_waitlist (position waitlistCount+1) if full, else book (spotsLeft). getPendingPromotions / acknowledgePromotions read and mark notices. index.ts re-exports the public API.","conventions":["Every mutation re-reads storage, builds the new state immutably, calls writeState, and only then updates memory and returns ok. If the write fails, return storage_failure and leave state unchanged (REQ-5, AC-42.3)","Methods accept a SessionRef or BookingRef (an id or an object with an id) and return BookingResult instead of throwing for rule violations","Rule thresholds (10 bookings, 168 h, 15 min, 2 h, 5 s undo) are named constants at the top of service.ts"],"dependsOn":["TASK-2"],"exemplars":["lib/booking/storage.ts","lib/booking/errors.ts"],"fileScope":["lib/booking/service.ts","lib/booking/filters.ts","lib/booking/index.ts"],"id":"TASK-3","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":780,"reqs":["REQ-6","REQ-7","REQ-8","REQ-9","REQ-10","REQ-11","REQ-13","REQ-14","REQ-15","REQ-16","REQ-17","REQ-18","REQ-19","REQ-21","REQ-22","REQ-25","REQ-26","REQ-27","REQ-28","REQ-30","REQ-31","REQ-34","REQ-60","REQ-63"],"title":"BookingService: rules, filters, lists, stats, action state, promotion hook"},{"approach":"local-api.ts: createLocalFetch(getService) returns a fetch-compatible function. It matches method + path under /api for every operation in the contract, parses JSON bodies and query params (type, intensity and timeOfDay are repeated params), calls the BookingService and answers with a Response. Session DTOs get the embedded instructor, endsAt, availabilityLabel, capacityLabel, actionState (including lateCancellation) and myBookingId. BookingRow DTOs get badge, canChange and session summary. BookingChange.message uses the design copy (\"You're booked for <name> · <Ddd> <HH:mm>\", \"Booking cancelled — <name>, <day> <HH:mm>\", and so on). Failure codes map as follows: not_found→404, invalid_request→400, storage_failure→500, every rule code→409 with {code, message, session?}, and class_full includes the refreshed session. If the service constructor throws, the answer is 500 storage_failure, and the service is rebuilt on the next call so Retry works. api-client.ts creates the generated lib/api client with baseUrl '/api' and fetch set to createLocalFetch(lazy client-side singleton service over browserStorage()). Shared hooks: useApiQuery (loading/error/data/retry), useOptimisticAction (apply a local patch at once, call the client, roll back and show an error toast on non-2xx or exception; a pending guard ignores repeat taps, NFR-7), errorCopy(code, serverMessage) gives plain-language toast text (overlap and limit messages come through as is), usePromotionToast (on mount, list the notices, show an info toast per notice, then acknowledge so each shows once; call it from every container), url-state (parse and serialise day, week, types, intensities, timesOfDay, tab, from and session in search params so Back restores state, REQ-44).","conventions":["Follow contracts/openapi.yaml exactly: paths, operationIds, status codes and DTO field names","Containers import only the generated client from lib/api (through api-client.ts), never lib/booking/service directly","No request ever leaves the browser (NFR-12); the user never sees raw error text (NFR-8)"],"dependsOn":["TASK-3"],"exemplars":["contracts/openapi.yaml","lib/booking/service.ts"],"fileScope":["lib/booking/local-api.ts","lib/booking/api-client.ts","components/screens/shared/use-api-query.ts","components/screens/shared/use-optimistic-action.ts","components/screens/shared/error-copy.ts","components/screens/shared/use-promotion-toast.ts","components/screens/shared/url-state.ts"],"id":"TASK-4","newFileKind":true,"plannedLoc":420,"reqs":["REQ-1","REQ-24","REQ-42","REQ-43"],"title":"Contract adapter: local fetch serving openapi.yaml, generated-client wiring, shared screen hooks"},{"approach":"Load getSession(sessionId) through useApiQuery. Show the generated loading state while loading, and the error state with Retry on 500. On 404 show the error copy with Back. Map the Session DTO to the hero (type accent), date, start–end, duration, room, instructor card, description, what to bring, availability block (aria-label from capacityLabel) and the free-cancellation note. Footer comes from actionState: book → 'Book this class' plus 'N spots left'; join_waitlist → 'You'd be #N'; booked → destructive 'Cancel booking' plus \"You're booked\"; waitlisted → 'Leave waitlist' plus \"You're #N on the waitlist\" and the skipReason message next to it (REQ-23); disabled → disabled button plus reason; canChange=false → disabled button plus reason. Book calls createBooking with an optimistic footer change and shows the success toast with an Undo button for 5 s (undoBooking). On 409 restore, show the rule message inline and as a toast. On class_full, replace the session with error.session so the footer becomes Join waitlist (REQ-48). Join and Leave show toasts without Undo. Cancel opens the confirmation dialog, which shows the late warning text when actionState.lateCancellation is true. Confirming calls cancelBooking. Dismissing changes nothing and returns focus to the trigger. Export the container with optional props variant ('page'|'panel') and onClose so S-1 can embed it as the desktop side panel. Back goes to the from/returnTo URL kept by url-state (Schedule day, week and filters, or the My Bookings tab), and falls back to '/'. Call usePromotionToast().","conventions":["Give the generated page real data and behaviour only: do not restyle or rebuild its blocks, states, overlays or text","'use client'; data comes only through the generated lib/api client","Use the kit's Dialog and toast (focus trap, Escape, focus returns to the trigger)"],"dependsOn":["TASK-4"],"exemplars":["components/screens/s-2/container.tsx","app/classes/[sessionId]/page.tsx"],"fileScope":["components/screens/s-2/container.tsx","components/screens/s-2/use-class-detail.ts"],"id":"TASK-5","newFileKind":false,"plannedLoc":340,"reqs":["REQ-23","REQ-41","REQ-42","REQ-44","REQ-45","REQ-46","REQ-47","REQ-48","REQ-55","REQ-56","REQ-57","REQ-58"],"title":"S-2 Class detail container: real data, footer actions, dialogs, rejections"},{"approach":"Read day, week and filters from url-state, defaulting to today. Call getSchedule(date, type[], intensity[], timeOfDay[]) through useApiQuery. Render days (7 chips 'Mon 12', today highlighted, empty days dimmed). The previous/next arrows follow canGoPreviousWeek/canGoNextWeek, and the Today button resets. Type chips, intensity and time-of-day are multi-select. Clear filters resets all three. States: skeleton cards while loading; 'No classes on this day' when no sessions and no filters; 'No classes match your filters' plus Clear filters when filters remove everything; the inline error with Retry on 500. Cards show the DTO fields with availabilityLabel and the capacity bar aria-label from capacityLabel. Studio-cancelled cards are struck through. The button label comes from actionState (Book / Join waitlist / Booked ✓ / Waitlisted #N) and is disabled for disabled kinds. Booked ✓ and Waitlisted #N buttons open Class Detail and never create a booking. Book uses useOptimisticAction: switch the card to Booked ✓ with an optimistic label, call createBooking, then replace the card with response.session and show the toast \"You're booked for <name> · <Ddd> <HH:mm>\" with Undo for 5 s (undoBooking restores the card). On failure restore the card and show the errorCopy toast. Join waitlist works the same with no Undo. Opening a card below 1024 px pushes /classes/{id} with from=schedule and the current query. At 1024 px and up it sets ?session={id} and renders the S-2 container as variant='panel' beside the list. The AR avatar and the My bookings link go to /bookings. Call usePromotionToast().","conventions":["Give the generated page real data and behaviour only: do not restyle or rebuild its blocks, states or text","'use client'; data comes only through the generated lib/api client; filter, day and week state lives in the URL via url-state","Cards open detail on click and on Enter/Space outside the action button; the button stops propagation"],"dependsOn":["TASK-5"],"exemplars":["components/screens/s-1/container.tsx","app/page.tsx"],"fileScope":["components/screens/s-1/container.tsx","components/screens/s-1/use-schedule.ts"],"id":"TASK-6","newFileKind":false,"plannedLoc":380,"reqs":["REQ-1","REQ-24","REQ-33","REQ-35","REQ-36","REQ-37","REQ-38","REQ-39","REQ-40","REQ-41","REQ-42","REQ-43","REQ-44","REQ-55","REQ-56","REQ-58"],"title":"S-1 Schedule container: week strip, filters, cards, optimistic book/join, side panel"},{"approach":"Load getMember, getStats and getMyBookings through useApiQuery. Show skeleton rows while loading and the inline error with Retry on 500. The header shows the AR avatar, name and membership. Stat tiles come from Stats. The Upcoming tab renders groups (label heading, rows with time, name, type tag, instructor, room, badge). Each row gets Cancel (Booked) or Leave waitlist (Waitlisted), disabled with a reason when canChange is false. Empty state: 'No upcoming classes' plus a 'Browse schedule' button to '/'. The Past tab shows rows with badges Attended, Cancelled, Late cancel or Cancelled by studio. Empty state: 'Your class history will appear here.' Clicking a row (or Enter on it) opens /classes/{sessionId}?from=bookings&tab=…. Quick Cancel opens the same confirmation dialog as Class Detail: title 'Cancel <name>?', with the late warning when isLateIfCancelledNow is true. Confirming optimistically moves the row and then calls cancelBooking. On success refresh stats and lists and show the toast. Leave waitlist opens its confirm dialog and then calls leaveWaitlist. On failure roll back and show the errorCopy toast (invalid_booking_state uses the design's validation copy). Focus returns to the trigger after the dialog closes. Call usePromotionToast().","conventions":["Give the generated page real data and behaviour only: do not restyle or rebuild its blocks, overlays or text","'use client'; data comes only through the generated lib/api client; the selected tab lives in the URL (?tab=past)","Controls keep accessible names that match their visible labels (Cancel, Leave waitlist, Cancel booking, Browse schedule) so the separately written end-to-end test can drive Schedule → Yoga → Book → My Bookings → Cancel"],"dependsOn":["TASK-6"],"exemplars":["components/screens/s-3/container.tsx","app/bookings/page.tsx"],"fileScope":["components/screens/s-3/container.tsx","components/screens/s-3/use-my-bookings.ts"],"id":"TASK-7","newFileKind":false,"plannedLoc":300,"reqs":["REQ-28","REQ-30","REQ-39","REQ-41","REQ-42","REQ-47","REQ-49","REQ-50","REQ-55","REQ-57","REQ-61"],"title":"S-3 My bookings container: stats, U